{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1449180-creating-the-best-initial-d-mage","id":1449180,"title":"Creating the best Initial D Mage","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-05-21T03:55:47-07:00","id":1449180,"title":"Creating the best Initial D Mage","content":"Well, as the title suggests, go on and discuss your best drifting theories and what a Mage could get/ do to become the king of the road.<br /> <br /> I'd say that a Mage with Time/ Forces/ Matter and Spirit could become a beast in such a setting. Time and Forces to use during drifts, to gain more speed, so far and so forth. Matter and Spirit, upgrade your car easily and/ or build it from scratch with parts you create/ buy and Spirit to Awaken it. That should give -1 difficulty or 1 die to Drive rolls made with that specific car.<br /> <br /> What do you guys think?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13197-skeeper0","name":"Skeeper0","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-21T12:10:28-07:00","id":1449202,"title":"","content":"I like the idea of car magic since I saw this Vulgar awesomeness:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=WTNb04VkyZc\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=WTNb04VkyZc\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=WTNb04VkyZc\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=WTNb04VkyZc </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I think that the Spheres are mostly OK. Forces/ Matter are the basics that cover the car.<br /> <br /> Time it's more than asceleration alone - If you only want that, Forces can do physical asceleration. But Time can excel at attaining such speeds with <i>control</i>, and at not needing to reinforce the structure of the car so much. My understanding it's that Time doesn't make you go faster per se, but rather throws you out of synch with the rest of the world. Allowing you to take two steps when the rest takes ony one - so to speak.<br /> Time 1 can provide all kinds of little boosts too - perhaps combined with Forces it could allow you to &quot;time&quot; your maneuvers more perfectly<br /> <br /> Spirit it's more of an outlier: Having 3 Sphere levels for a minor buff isn't worth it (lots of ways to get bonuses in Mage). Spirit really shines if you're a shaman that it's going to comunicate with the car, race in the spirit worlds, commune with car totems and spirits (note: Spirit it's high on socialization. As an example, that -1 from Awakening can turn into a +1 if you mistreat the car).<br /> <br /> Other outliers could include:<br /> Correspondence: useful for checking the area and finding the best paths, and in higher levels to do crazy shenanigans like the car being bigger on the inside or traversing trough obstacles.<br /> Prime: to make the car - or instruments inside the car - into Wonder.<br /> <br /> Many Foucses could boost driving and cars. But I think the true master would have cars, and the Skill used to drive, be the Instrument","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-22T06:38:51-07:00","id":1449242,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1449180-creating-the-best-initial-d-mage?p=1449202#post1449202\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like the idea of car magic since I saw this Vulgar awesomeness:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=WTNb04VkyZc\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=WTNb04VkyZc\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=WTNb04VkyZc\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=WTNb04VkyZc </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I think that the Spheres are mostly OK. Forces/ Matter are the basics that cover the car.<br /> <br /> Time it's more than asceleration alone - If you only want that, Forces can do physical asceleration. But Time can excel at attaining such speeds with <i>control</i>, and at not needing to reinforce the structure of the car so much. My understanding it's that Time doesn't make you go faster per se, but rather throws you out of synch with the rest of the world. Allowing you to take two steps when the rest takes ony one - so to speak.<br /> Time 1 can provide all kinds of little boosts too - perhaps combined with Forces it could allow you to &quot;time&quot; your maneuvers more perfectly<br /> <br /> Spirit it's more of an outlier: Having 3 Sphere levels for a minor buff isn't worth it (lots of ways to get bonuses in Mage). Spirit really shines if you're a shaman that it's going to comunicate with the car, race in the spirit worlds, commune with car totems and spirits (note: Spirit it's high on socialization. As an example, that -1 from Awakening can turn into a +1 if you mistreat the car).<br /> <br /> Other outliers could include:<br /> Correspondence: useful for checking the area and finding the best paths, and in higher levels to do crazy shenanigans like the car being bigger on the inside or traversing trough obstacles.<br /> Prime: to make the car - or instruments inside the car - into Wonder.<br /> <br /> Many Foucses could boost driving and cars. But I think the true master would have cars, and the Skill used to drive, be the Instrument</div> </div> </div> </div>What about a Cloaking/ Arcane effect as per the Background? What would that possibly take? Correspondence to thicken the Space so that you pass unnoticed, Time to thicken the Timestream so that the Technocracy won't detect you on their Temporal Anomalies radar, Forces to literally cloak the car in camo, Matter to bind the whole effect to the car. Would you have any other ideas to this concept?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13197-skeeper0","name":"Skeeper0","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-22T08:57:37-07:00","id":1449258,"title":"","content":"Had an NPC like this in the Mage game I ran for years, a Tytalan whose car was her unique focus for Forces. Although, being her car was a '67 Shelby GT500, her range of activities in it wasn't so much centered around finesse so much as, frankly, weaponizing the car in as many ostentatious ways as possible. As a proper Tytalan should.<br /> <br /> But, even though that game ran a <i>long</i> time and she went on to become <i>damned</i> powerful, her initial sphere spread was considerably different from what has been mentioned so far: namely, she had far heavier investments into Mind and Entropy than Forces, Matter, or Time.<br /> <br /> Mind being great specifically for boosting Wits (the associated attribute with driving four-wheeled vehicles) and Drive (a skill), and rotes for improving reaction/reflex time or capacity to predict events in the immediate future -- Mind alone would suffice, but Life (using a physiological vector) or Time (obvious) being good conjunctional spheres for such an effect. Higher-level uses of Mind still apply, from something as simple as placing a &quot;get the hell out of my way&quot; impulse effect on the car, all the way to making the computational systems in any contemporary motor vehicle sentient (who needs Spirit to make KITT?).<br /> <br /> I found Entropy honestly to have a ton more uses in a wider range of scenes than Forces. You <i>could</i> theoretically bullshit your way into an &quot;I never hit red lights&quot; rote with Forces, but it's just easier and more elegant with Entropy. Same for more complex effects that manipulate traffic patterns, likelihood other drivers have wrecks or are particularly road rage-y that day, and the list goes on. One of this Tytalan's rotes, for example, was a &quot;Grand Theft Auto mode&quot; rote (Mind 2, Entropy 3) she deployed in chase scenes with traffic, that made third parties on the road spontaneously drive like absolute, road raging, lunatics -- foiling the actions of other parties to the chase.<br /> <br /> Also, that little skosh of Matter can be more useful than the surface level, or prototypical uses (armoring, super-powerful fuel) might imply. For example, werewolf versus car with silver bumper and grill. Never mind using Prime or Correspondence to convert headlights into &quot;real&quot; sunlight. The Tytalan NPC got <i>more</i> than ample use out of her &quot;high beams&quot; rote, specifically because one part of the chronicle involved dealing with a particularly troublesome Tytalan at a point when the PC's were <i>trying</i> to make friendly with some local Tremere to achieve a mutually-beneficial goal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-22T12:45:56-07:00","id":1449276,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Skeeper0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1449180-creating-the-best-initial-d-mage?p=1449242#post1449242\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What about a Cloaking/ Arcane effect as per the Background? What would that possibly take? Correspondence to thicken the Space so that you pass unnoticed, Time to thicken the Timestream so that the Technocracy won't detect you on their Temporal Anomalies radar, Forces to literally cloak the car in camo, Matter to bind the whole effect to the car. Would you have any other ideas to this concept?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, Matter to lock, if we go with M20, it's useful - of course.<br /> <br /> I think Mind 2/3 &quot;ignore this car, it's just a car like any other in spite of all the crazy driving&quot; it's the most Arcane thing you can have w/o Entropy 5. As <i>Theodrim </i>suggested, you could look at Mind and Entropy instead...at chargen it's a way to get cheap driving bonuses, and you get the potential to make your car to be Arcane-ish as a bonus<br /> <br /> Time it's a hard &quot;no&quot; in my opinion. Time cloacks prevent other mages from scrying you from a different point in time, but that in itself leaves a trace. Mages will be more suspicious if they &quot;can't&quot; check the timestream where your car passes than if they can and see some crazy driving - because that's usually a sign of a wizard doing something bad. Time shading it's for when you're better served by the enemy knowing you're hiding something than to risk them knowing <i>what </i>you're doing.<br /> <br /> Correspondence it's doable, but I think you need 4 to fold space that way around a car.<br /> <br /> If you like Spirit, at 4 you could drive through the Penumbra instead (traversing the spirit wilds with a cadillac sounds like all sorts of fun - but would be it's own adventure...)<br /> <br /> Forces to make your car invisible it's the easy one, that can be achieved from chargen. But an invisible car (that also makes the ppl inside, invisible, of course) sounds like it would be a pain to drive w/o Mind/Entropy (or Correspondence 4/5) to deal with the trafic.<br /> <br /> If you build this from Chargen, buying the car as a Talisman with the Wonder Background could be a good idea to save on Spheres and/or allow some Effects you can't have with Spheres at 3 max.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-22T18:52:01-07:00","id":1449299,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1449180-creating-the-best-initial-d-mage?p=1449276#post1449276\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If you build this from Chargen, buying the car as a Talisman with the Wonder Background could be a good idea to save on Spheres and/or allow some Effects you can't have with Spheres at 3 max.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is an issue I ran into with this specific NPC as well. Cars...aren't exactly small, nor are they maintenance-free or impervious to damage. An entire car may not be the best-possible thing to make a Talisman, especially for the fairly ludicrous point-cost value it would nominally have just to get it do to the things you might want it to do. We're talking &quot;pooled background&quot; point level, unless the player is willing to blow all their freebies on it and just start with Arete 1 -- the Wonder motor vehicles in the NWO splatbook <i>start</i> at eight points, before any additional goodies that do what player will want to do are added to it.<br /> <br /> A smart and cheaper option is to buy multiple Wonders as <i>car component</i> artifacts and charms, not talismans. For example, an engine block that never needs fluid change or never breaks down, or has magically-enhanced horsepower and torque; a set of tires that never go flat and or have controllable road friction and rolling resistance; a glasspack that packs the &quot;get the hell out of my way&quot; effect; if your mage is an asshole, a coal roller that creates magical smoke screens; or, a case of &quot;special&quot; oil, fuel additive, or nitrous canisters that provide on-demand performance improvement (charm).<br /> <br /> Or for the EV-minded, a battery pack that's conveniently home to an electricity elemental which means the car never has to be charged, or it can be charged on demand (fetish). The last one's something I did in a VtM game, playing this woo-woo, high humanity, hippie Telyav who had Spirit Thaumaturgy and an unlife goal of meeting and befriending every spirit she could against all odds. So naturally, an electricity elemental ally was a natural, achievable, goal to meet since she was an EV driver.<br /> <br /> This way you can mix and match in accordance to your starting sphere spread, and shore up weaknesses while building upon strengths, cost-effectively. It also has the spin-off benefit that if the vehicle itself is totaled (a real hazard), the Wonder can be retrieved and installed into another car. Or if the mage simply gets a new car, the Wonder can potentially be moved from the old vehicle to the new.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":431,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","user":"Theodrim","date":". 05-22-2021, 10:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-22T20:06:47-07:00","id":1449304,"title":"","content":"I feel compelled to mention the Stephen King short story &quot;Mrs. Todd's Shortcut&quot;, in which the title character's obsession with finding shortcuts results in being able to drive from one place to another in fewer miles than are directly between them on a map. And at that point, things get ... weird. It's an interesting example of someone bending space-time (to the point of possible dimensional travel) simply out of pure obsession to do so. (That or finding secret lost &quot;faerie roads&quot;.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-23T03:22:08-07:00","id":1449334,"title":"","content":"Thanks for everything! I've taken notes and I will now annoy my ST to bits. Looking forward to more ideas.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13197-skeeper0","name":"Skeeper0","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-26T19:48:11-07:00","id":1449741,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1449180-creating-the-best-initial-d-mage?p=1449304#post1449304\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel compelled to mention the Stephen King short story &quot;Mrs. Todd's Shortcut&quot;, in which the title character's obsession with finding shortcuts results in being able to drive from one place to another in fewer miles than are directly between them on a map. And at that point, things get ... weird. It's an interesting example of someone bending space-time (to the point of possible dimensional travel) simply out of pure obsession to do so. (That or finding secret lost &quot;faerie roads&quot;.)</div> </div> </div> </div>The Explorators were doing something similar to this as far back as The Sorcerer's Crusade, so this checks out. Employing advanced understanding of Correspondence to &quot;find shortcuts&quot;, making trips faster than they logically should be. All without incurring Paradox, because it happens over distances and times too large for any single observer to grasp that something unnatural is happening.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-26T19:53:20-07:00","id":1449744,"title":"","content":"I'm still sad the Arthaus Sorcerers Crusade line ended before we got the planned Explorers Guide.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-26T19:58:35-07:00","id":1449747,"title":"","content":"One way to employ Life in a car would be to combine it with Matter or Forces, to convert organic materials into fuel. A grisly version of this is seen in the short-lived TV series <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blood_Drive_(TV_series)\" target=\"_blank\">Blood Drive</a>, but a tamer version can be found in the Back To The Future films with Doc Brown's upgraded DeLorean being able to power its time travel device using mundane organic waste. (Though, plot critically for the third film, not its engines, which still run on gas).<br /> <br /> While we're on the subject of grindhouse movies, though, a Mage might employ Entropy, Matter, Forces, and/or Life to make a <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Death_Proof\" target=\"_blank\">Death Proof</a> car. At least, for the one in the driver seat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-26T20:06:07-07:00","id":1449748,"title":"","content":"Simon R. Green's Nightside novels makes frequent mention of the idea of vehicles which run on blood, souls, and other esoteric materials, though I think the only vehicle that ever finally gets fully explained is one character's car which turns out to be some sort of advanced sentient cyber tech weapon that rebelled from its creators and ran (drove?) off to do its own thing. I've honestly always kind of wanted to do a Virtual Adept that was a riff on Knight Rider, who came into possession of a renegade/escaped ItX experimental vehicle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}